  "illustration_prompt": "Create a single publication-quality landscape 3:2 narrative illustration for an adult illustrated English-reading booklet. Finished standalone artwork, not a book mockup, not a collage of multiple unrelated panels. Sophisticated contemporary editorial gouache and watercolor, carefully controlled colored-pencil accents, velvety matte paint, subtle warm paper texture, soft natural daylight. Warm ivory paper dominates; subdued eucalyptus and sage greens structure the composition; restrained buttery lemon-yellow and dusty terracotta accents. Calm, comfortable, refined, credible drawing and natural anatomy. An airy coherent composition with one clear story focal point and at most two supporting details, generous breathing room at all edges and softly feathered painted edges into ivory. Detailed but uncluttered. Historically and scientifically appropriate objects, clothing and setting. Show the particular article's pivotal event or mechanism rather than a generic portrait or generic textbook symbols. Human figures treated with dignity; no grotesque caricature, no sensational violence or visible injuries. For disasters, emphasize the setting, evidence or human response without graphic suffering. For uncertain scientific claims, depict the observations and investigation without presenting debated mechanisms as proven. Absolutely no typography, captions, letters, numbers, logos, watermarks, diagram labels, fake writing or invented charts anywhere. Do not render invisible forces as literal magic. Avoid corporate vector icons, slick 3D rendering and childish cartoon style. High-quality, print-ready visual storytelling, matching a warm ivory-and-sage adult watercolor booklet.\n\nARTICLE62: A quiet scientifically grounded Roslin farm nursery in Scotland in 1996. The focal event is a small healthy white-faced Finn Dorset lamb, Dolly, standing beside the Blackface ewe that carried her as a surrogate; the surrogate has unmistakably dark face and legs, white fleece, and a natural sheep head. The white lamb is physically separate, white face clearly visible, not an identical black-faced copy of the surrogate. A restrained hint of a simple farm laboratory doorway in soft background can suggest research, without syringes, floating cells, genetics diagrams, halos or magical duplication. One coherent rural setting, warm gentle daylight and dignity. Natural proportions and four legs on each sheep, soft realistic wool, no labels or branding.",
